 bool ShunkoTargetIsPrivate(const CService& target)
 {
+    // Shunko's whole premise is that the last hop is a hidden service, so the
+    // target has to be one. Asking only whether a proxy is configured is not the
+    // same question: GetProxy() answers for whatever network the address belongs
+    // to, and a global -proxy is configured for all of them. A clearnet IPv4
+    // target therefore passed the old check and the hand-over went out through a
+    // Tor exit, which is an observer with no reason to protect the sender.
+    if (!target.IsPrivacyNet()) return false;
